{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Stormbringer: Never Strikes Twice? repeats Electrocute at the cast rank (#3450)",
  "contract": "#3450 Never Strikes Twice? (804828) is SPELL_ATTR0_PASSIVE with ProcChance 25, Spell.dbc ProcFlags 0 and one effect: SPELL_EFFECT_APPLY_AURA with EffectApplyAuraName 42 (SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL) on EffectTriggerSpell 801844. With no spell_proc row, SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs skipped the record ('Skip if no proc flags in DBC') and Aura::GetProcEffectMask returned 0 ('only auras with spell proc entry can trigger proc'), so 'Your Electrocute now has a 25% chance to strike again' never happened. A spell_proc row alone would not deliver the tooltip either: 801844 is Electrocute Rank 1 and AuraEffect::HandleProcTriggerSpellAuraProc casts the literal EffectTriggerSpell with no rank resolution, while spell_ranks and the module's own progression give a level 80 Stormbringer Rank 13 (501432), so the repeat would land at Rank 1 damage. The fix therefore performs the roll in the class's existing AllSpellScript OnSpellHitResult hook, gated on the passive being known, on the damaging spell being in Electrocute's rank chain and on the hit not being triggered - the same guard the Electrocutioner proc beside it uses, which also prevents the repeat from re-triggering itself - and re-casts the rank that actually procced. The discriminator is a cast count: 24 deliberate casts with the passive must produce more than 24 Electrocutes, and none of them may be Rank 1. No absolute damage number is asserted, because Electrocute's damage depends on spell power and on spell_bonus_data rows that PR #4612 is still restoring. A damage-landed assertion (spell_damage_count 501432 on dummy) was tried and dropped in postfix debugging (2026-09-22): spell_cast_count is a server-side counter (ProcCounter::RecordCast, hooked to AllSpellScript::OnSpellCast, which Spell::cast() fires once handle_immediate() has already run) that increments once the cast reaches that point regardless of whether any target's effect survived per-target exclusion in Spell::AddUnitTarget/CheckEffectTarget, while spell_damage_count only counts an actual non-zero SMSG_SPELLNONMELEEDAMAGELOG. A run recorded 37 casts against only 30 logged damage events, including attrition on the guaranteed-good baseline/deliberate casts, with no cast rejection (cast_failures null) and no miss/resist mathematically possible against this fixture (zero average resistance at equal level, hit chance capped by 10000 hit rating, non-lethal ~1048-1114 damage against 300000 HP). No source-level mechanism for the gap was established; it is independent of the #3450 fix, so no damage-count threshold is asserted here. That run used a Rabbit (721) fixture. The enemy is now a Harvest Golem (36): CritterAI::JustEngagedWith puts a damaged critter into a timed flee, and Electrocute carries FacingCasterFlags 1, so a baseline cast was rejected with SPELL_FAILED_UNIT_NOT_INFRONT (134) once the fleeing Rabbit left the caster's front arc; the baseline then counted 7 Electrocutes instead of 8, and every rejected talented cast is a lost 25% roll.",
  "timeout_ms": 240000,
